    "problem_statement": "On a POSIX platform without kernel IPv6 multicast routing (MRT6), there is no way to forward Backbone Router multicast traffic between the Thread interface and the infrastructure interface in userspace. The forwarding policy that decides whether an IPv6 packet may be forwarded (rejecting non-IPv6, unicast, sub-admin-local scope, and multicast/unspecified/loopback/link-local sources, and hop limits below the minimum), plus the duplicate suppression, the per-group/total rate limiting, and the Ethernet frame construction used to inject forwarded packets, are not available. Implement this userspace multicast forwarding logic so that the new interface for the forwarder's packet checks, duplicate cache, token-bucket rate limiter, and Ethernet frame builder is present and behaves as specified.",
